good morning and thank you for coming  my name is john pelletier i'm a captain  with the las vegas metropolitan police  department  and i oversee the major violator and  narcotics bureau  we're here this morning because of the  alarming increase that this community  has seen  in overdose deaths last year last year  alone we had a 30 percent increase  from 591 to  768.  what's even more shocking is we had just  under a 2  200 percent increase in fentanyl  related deaths from 74  to 219  to put it in perspective in august alone  we had 31 deaths that is  a death a day from fentanyl  this emergency this situation  does not discriminate it does not care  how old you are  it does not care where you live we have  responded to teenagers  we have responded to the elderly you can  see from the map  right here all the places in this  community that we have gone  what's truly horrible about this is it's  completely preventable  every single one of these did not have  to happen  one bad pill will  kill again one bad pill  will kill if you are not prescribed  that drug from a pharmacist and doctor  do not take it  fentanyl is often disguised as a  prescription pill  but it can be up to 100 times  more potent than morphine or heroin  people that die from fentanyl  believe they are taking a prescription  grade pill  but they are taking a street or  pressed pill that was made who knows  where  with who knows what and the bottom line  is  they didn't know what they were taking  if you look  you can see a mixture of  press pills real pills they look real  enough  and what people don't understand is that  amount next to the penny  is what it takes to be fatal  because of this local law enforcement  and prosecutors came together to create  the overdose  response team members of the team  along with lvmpd include the district  attorney  the u.s attorney the dea  the coroner's office nevada haida  henderson hsi  we came together and the mission of the  overdose response team is to reduce  fatal and non-fatal overdose instances  to develop investigative leads to help  find those that are perpetrating this  and to prosecute them  and please understand we are working  with local and federal  prosecutors so that we can do the  absolute most  possible and if possible we will charge  you with murder  and a minimum for that is 20-year  sentence  also if you or someone  you know has a substance abuse problem  please seek help before it's too late  there are multiple resources available  if you need to know where they are you  can simply go to lvmpd.com  click on the resource or helpful link  and the we care booklet  do not allow a loved one or yourself  to become a statistic if you know  someone selling  or manufacturing illegal narcotics  and you wish to remain anonymous you can  call crime stoppers at 702-385-5555  thank you  so in 2019 you had 591 overdose deaths  in 2020 you had 768.  in 2019 fentanyl deaths you had 74  in 2020 you had 219.  so far this year not good i mean just  that's why we're here it's it's  if you knew an intersection had a death  a day at that intersection the public  would be screaming  what are we doing we had a death a day  for fentanyl  in august and so we're coming together  screaming  do not take those pills  sir  one can certainly make the argument that  you're staying at home  but the problem is these  precursors are available and people are  using them to manufacture  the the press pills do you want to make  an argument that  it the shutdown made it easier i don't  know that we have enough information  we've seen a trend  coming for several years but it's make  no mistake we said fentanyl was coming  fentanyl is here  okay thank you
 

